# What git keeps of a project folder (for example bruce_lee/):
#   releases/       the release files as you got them (original/ in projects before c64-re-tools 2.7)
#   .c64-re-tools/knowledge/   the knowledge
#   src/            the generated source, identical to the image
#   docs/           the written pages and the generated reference
#   runs/, tests/   the runs (run.json, results and coverage maps) and the scenarios
#   tools/
# Everything below is installed, machine-local, regenerated or scratch.

# Installed by the skills installer: install again on each computer.
.claude/
.ap-sdk/
.mcp.json
# The ASD-STE100 skill: npx skills add danyuchn/asd-ste100-skill -y
.agents/
skills-lock.json

# Machine-local state: the knowledge index, one-time batches and step files,
# and SQLite files of a write in progress.
**/.c64-re-tools/local/
**/.c64-re-tools/*.db-journal
**/.c64-re-tools/*.db-wal
**/.c64-re-tools/*.db-shm

# Regenerated output.
# build/: tools/build.sh writes the PRGs and the assembler results (the tests need them).
build/
snapshots/

# Copies and archives in the top folder: the input disk belongs in <project>/releases/.
/*.d64
/*.d71
/*.d81
/*.g64
/*.crt
/*.tap
/*.t64
/*.prg
/*.zip

# Python, Node and editor scratch.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
node_modules/
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
